  "_readme": "Golden vectors for the device control backend token, the signing keys record, the command envelope and sealed payloads, from docs/architecture-decisions/companion-app-authentication.md. Each implementation (the Home Assistant integration, the Homey app, the Zendo app) copies this file into its tests and checks every case. Every key below is a test key only: never use one anywhere else. Tests inject `now` as the current time and `linkedSiteId` as the hub's linked site, and read the signing keys from `keysRecord`. Token `expect` is valid or invalid, and `registration` is what v2 registration answers for it: accept, or the error code. Envelope `expect` is accept, refuse (answer the command with an error) or drop (not for this device), for the device in `device`. Sealed payload `expect` is accept or refuse. Every ecies-p256 case gives its fixed one-off key and nonce, and the intermediates, under `inputs`, so an implementation can reproduce the exact bytes when sealing.",
